WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.670
Reflective practice is structured learning from experience.

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:07.442
It is the deliberate habit of looking at real work, asking what happened,

00:00:07.442 --> 00:00:11.114
examining the evidence, and deciding what should change next time.

00:00:11.114 --> 00:00:15.519
Experience gives raw material, but reflection turns that material into reusable learning.

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:16.253
Without reflection,

00:00:16.253 --> 00:00:20.659
a person can repeat the same activity many times while carrying forward

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:22.494
the same assumptions and mistakes.

00:00:22.494 --> 00:00:25.798
Reflection is different from memory, reaction, analysis, and rumination.

00:00:25.798 --> 00:00:27.267
Memory recalls an event.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.469
Reaction expresses how the event felt.

00:00:29.469 --> 00:00:31.672
Analysis breaks the event into parts.

00:00:31.672 --> 00:00:34.242
Reflection connects the event to future action.

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:38.647
It asks what the experience reveals about decisions, assumptions, context, tradeoffs, skills,

00:00:38.647 --> 00:00:39.749
systems, and behavior.

00:00:39.749 --> 00:00:42.686
The purpose is not to relive the past;

00:00:42.686 --> 00:00:45.256
it is to improve the next attempt.

00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:48.560
Reflective practice matters in technical work, learning, leadership, communication,

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.395
incident response, and skill development.

00:00:50.395 --> 00:00:53.332
A developer can reflect on a debugging session.

00:00:53.332 --> 00:00:55.902
A team can reflect after an incident.

00:00:55.902 --> 00:00:58.839
A leader can reflect after a difficult conversation.

00:00:58.839 --> 00:01:01.042
A learner can reflect after practice.

00:01:01.042 --> 00:01:02.143
In each case,

00:01:02.143 --> 00:01:08.017
the point is to notice patterns that would otherwise remain hidden inside the pace of work.

00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:10.954
This course treats reflection as practical and non-clinical.

00:01:10.954 --> 00:01:14.625
It is not vague journaling, performative note-taking, blame, or self-criticism.

00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:18.296
It is also not a reason to delay action forever.

00:01:18.296 --> 00:01:23.436
The goal is to turn real work into reusable learning: better questions, better judgment,

00:01:23.436 --> 00:01:26.740
better habits, better systems, and more reliable future performance.
